WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.970
Drop a small ball into a tall
tube of thick, syrupy fluid.

2
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.020
Here, the resistive force grows
in step with the ball's speed:

3
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.030
twice as fast, twice the push back.

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.630
As the ball speeds up, it
heads towards a terminal speed,

5
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.780
where the net force would be zero.

6
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.930
Does it ever actually get there?

7
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.990
Or only ever get closer?

8
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.050
In this mission, you'll turn the second
law into a differential equation for the

9
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.410
falling ball.

10
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.170
Then you'll solve it by
separating the variables,

11
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.910
and see how the speed changes with time.

12
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.510
Your mission: decide whether the falling
ball ever truly reaches its terminal

13
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.240
speed, and prove it.
